{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for leased activity status and bounded multi-event focus at exact clean head e8ee5ccdb8a0e597e3ca99cb1e44f0d9e2d97b29 on request/leased-activity-focus. Reviewed in a detached scratch worktree at that exact commit; the head did not move during the review (branch and artifact still name e8ee5cc, main still dfa5117).\n\nThe behaviour is right. Every claim the request names is correct at this head, and the gates pass: go vet clean, go test ./... all 15 packages ok, go test -race ./... all 15 packages ok, go build ./... clean, 53 of 53 UI tests pass, make ui-check clean, and three fresh builds from an emptied internal/service/uidist produce byte-identical trees that match the committed embed. Activity never reaches a durable layer: it appears in no file under internal/kernel, internal/workroom, internal/statusview or cmd/gs, and handleAnnounce only reads a workspace snapshot. Announce renewals preserve activity and do not advance the live cursor; an activity transition appends one typed change carried by wait; expiry removes status and focus with the lease; the private session identifier stays the authority boundary and a published handle announces a separate lease rather than mutating the original; the MCP presence tool copies only status, focus and note from tool arguments, so a supplied actor or session cannot displace adapter custody; multi-session aggregation is order-independent, because taking the eight smallest of a growing union discards only members that could not have survived the final cut. The thread railway is untouched here and stays bounded at ten lanes with an honest folded lane, so the unbounded width measured in verdict c4fd4e4c does not return. Whoami's seven orientation tests pass unchanged.\n\nThe pins are what fall short. I applied 25 single-change mutations at this exact head, each alone and reverted immediately; 21 turned the suite red. Five did not, and three of them sit on conditions this request names.\n\nFinding 1, bound values are pinned only against themselves. TestLeasedActivityRejectsUnboundedOrInvalidInput builds its oversized input from the constant it is testing (MaxFocusEvents+1, MaxActivityNoteBytes+1), so changing MaxFocusEvents from 8 to 9, or MaxActivityNoteBytes from 160 to 400, leaves the entire Go suite green. The number eight is also stated in SKILL.md, docs/reference.md and AGENTS.md, advertised as maxItems in the MCP schema, and hardcoded four times as slice(0, 8) in TypeScript. Concretely: a later edit raises MaxFocusEvents to 12, every gate stays green, the MCP schema advertises 12, and the browser silently truncates the aggregated focus of any actor back to 8, so an agent that focuses 12 events is displayed as focusing 8 while the documented \"at most eight\" has quietly become false.\n\nFinding 2, two bounds have no assertion at all. Deleting \"len(event) \u003e MaxFocusEventBytes || !utf8.ValidString(event)\" from normalizeActivity leaves the whole suite green: neither the 256-byte per-event limit nor the UTF-8 validity check is pinned anywhere. It is not reachable through the service today, because the workroom-EventID check is pinned and rejects anything that is not a known EventID, but nexus is a package boundary with its own tests and the request asks for all input bounds.\n\nFinding 3, the Stream focus indicator is not pinned behaviourally. Wrapping all three \"\u003cFocusActors actors={focused} /\u003e\" call sites in Stream.tsx so they never render leaves all 53 UI tests green; the indicator can be deleted in silence. Its only pin is a regex over the source text asserting the computation exists. That regex also fails in the other direction: rewriting focus.includes(statement.event) to focus.indexOf(statement.event) \u003e= 0, which is the same behaviour, turns the suite red. The WorkDrawer indicator is pinned properly, through rendered markup, so the pattern to follow is already in the file.\n\nTwo smaller gaps, offered rather than required. Nothing asserts that an activity update leaves the durable frontier unchanged, which is the request's first claim; TestPresenceActivityUsesTheLeaseAndCompositeWait already holds \"before\" and could compare Durable.Head after the update in one line. And making cloneActivity return the hub's internal slice instead of a copy leaves everything green, so the copy that keeps a Snapshot caller from mutating hub state is unpinned, in a file that clones keys, genesis and payloads deliberately everywhere else. Separately, the server's own focus-count check is fully redundant with the nexus check; removing it changes only the error message.\n\nTo close: pin the two bound values against literals rather than against themselves, add nexus assertions for a 257-byte focus event and an invalid-UTF-8 focus event, and pin the Stream indicator through rendered markup while loosening the source regex so a semantics-preserving refactor does not fail. That is additive; no production change is needed, and the implementation itself reads as correct.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0be172538ea08858bf5950d699eb3c8d916924c0","head":"e8ee5ccdb8a0e597e3ca99cb1e44f0d9e2d97b29","verdict":"changes-requested"}}